From: oscmix-autostart
Subject: [PATCH] device_ffucxii: take the Room EQ offset relative to the base

The Room EQ block starts at 0x35D0, which is not 32-aligned -- its low
five bits are 0x10. Recombining the per-output offset with `|` therefore
collides for offsets 16..31, folding the upper half of each output's
block onto its lower half: 0x35E0 (BAND5FREQ) decodes as 0x35D0 (DELAY),
0x35E3 (BAND6FREQ) as 0x35D3 (BAND1GAIN), and so on.

On a Fireface UCX II this makes 320 registers unreachable and reports
260 of them under another name, so a single /refresh carries two
conflicting values for the same OSC path.

Measured before and after on hardware (serial 24216011): the dump goes
from 1932 registers with 260 conflicting paths to 2252 with none, and
bands 6 to 9 become visible with plausible values.

See michaelforney/oscmix#32.
---
--- a/device_ffucxii.c
+++ b/device_ffucxii.c
@@ -121,7 +121,7 @@
 	} else if (reg - 0x35D0U < 0x280) {
 		p->out = (reg - 0x35D0) >> 5;
-		reg = 0x35D0 | (reg & 0x1F);
+		reg = 0x35D0 + ((reg - 0x35D0) & 0x1F);
 	}
 	switch (reg) {
